   <h1>HWvH support</h1>
-  <p>Developer: Nathan Fennel. Updated October 3, 2026.</p>
-  <h2>Build, then race</h2>
-  <p>Pick a player, make a character, customize a car and build a track. Use the play button to try your creation. Close the preview to return to the workshop. Save profiles, characters, cars and tracks on the device where you create them.</p>
+  <p>Developer: Nathan Fennel. Updated October 4, 2026.</p>
+  <h2>Play right away</h2>
+  <p>Choose PLAY! on the opening screen to race a starter car and track against a robot. Choosing or creating a player is optional. For your own designs, pick a player, make a character, customize a car and build a track. Use the play button to try your creation, then close the preview to return to the workshop. Save profiles, characters, cars and tracks on the device where you create them.</p>
+  <h2>Rematch or share a finish</h2>
+  <p>When a race ends, choose REMATCH! to race again, or SHARE to prepare an image of the actual finished arena with the final results and an App Store link. On iPad, choose Share Image to open the system sharing sheet. Closing the sheet returns to the same finished race; starting a rematch does not change an image already prepared.</p>
+  <p>For a standalone Apple TV race, open SHARE on the TV, then Race on TV on a nearby iPad to receive the image. The temporary sharing connection is available while the TV's share panel is open. A race already using connected iPads sends the image over that race connection. On a connected iPad, Get Race Image requests the same finish again if the image is not ready; once it arrives, choose Share Race. If preparation fails, keep the finished race open and try again.</p>
   <h2>Use the Siri Remote</h2>
   <p>Move focus and select an action to edit tracks, decorations, car styles and characters on Apple TV. Menu returns from the current screen. A connected keyboard can help with names.</p>
   <p>In the car's Draw section, select the pen control to switch between Pen Up and Pen Down. With the pen down, select direction buttons to draw. Lift the pen to move without making a mark. Choose an ink color and brush width, or use Eraser and Clear Drawing to remove marks.</p>
   <h2>Race with nearby iPads</h2>
   <p>Open local multiplayer on Apple TV, then choose Race on TV on the iPad. Allow Local Network when your device asks. Choose a car and tracks, then ready up. Keep the devices nearby on a network that allows local peer connections.</p>
   <p>If discovery fails, check Local Network access in Settings. Guest or managed Wi-Fi networks may isolate devices. Standalone building and racing remain available without local multiplayer.</p>
+  <h2>Choose the game feel</h2>
+  <p>Open Settings from the opening screen or workshop. Animation and Haptics start on and save independently on each device. Turn Animation off for calmer world motion, buttons and cameras. The app also respects the device's Reduce Motion setting. Haptics controls tap and boost feedback on supported iPads. Race timing, physics and controls stay the same.</p>
   <h2>The iPad camera is optional</h2>
   <p>Take a photo only when you want the app to pick your character colors. The app analyzes the picture on the iPad and does not save it in your app library or upload it. You can always choose colors manually. Apple Pencil drawing is available on iPad; Apple TV uses its remote pen controls.</p>
